  },
  "body": "Meta Muse's app, authentication/API hosts and dedicated VM hosts currently fall through to FINAL → Global. Add `DOMAIN-SUFFIX,muse.ai` and `DOMAIN-SUFFIX,metaaivm.com` to the persistent Manual AI input and regenerate the AI rules, manifest, Clash mirror and receipts. Exactly two rules are added; no existing rule is removed or moved. Existing `meta.ai` AI routing and shared `auth.meta.com` SocialMedia routing remain covered by regression tests.\n\nEvidence:\n- [Meta's announcement](https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/) links muse.ai, introducing.muse.ai and security.muse.ai; the app redirects to auth.muse.ai.\n- The [public Muse client](https://muse.ai/_next/static/chunks/2ql8nnti3ddjq.js) exports `FEATHER_VM_HOST_SUFFIX = \".metaaivm.com\"` and recognizes UUID VM hostnames. The [app bundle](https://muse.ai/_next/static/chunks/0vvf6a_0u6xew.js) references api.muse.ai.\n- Before the change, active Surge rule evaluation returned FINAL for the Muse app/auth/API and VM gateway hosts. This is a rule evaluation, not proof of an authenticated Muse session.\n\nValidation: seven new coverage cases fail on the old rules and pass after generation; 141 routing cases and 69 unit tests pass. Repository/override contracts, receipt consistency, Clash validation and whitespace checks pass. Online audit: 41 sources, 0 errors, 0 warnings, six existing informational notices. Global was regenerated to honor the dependency contract; its body was identical, so its unchanged snapshot was retained.\n",
